or floor briefly steadies beneath the figure's feet where it meets the gold handrail. The stable contact reframes support as an environmental condition for continuing, not proof of incapacity.","mode":"metaphor","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C04-B08","script_section":"S4","visual_information":"The figure leans slightly toward the handrail while keeping both shoulders upright and balanced. The controlled lean shows support being used without rescue or loss of dignity.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C04-B09","script_section":"S4","visual_information":"The distant second presence remains peripheral as the figure advances beside the handrail rather than being pulled forward. The composition separates companionship from dependence.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C04-B10","script_section":"S4","visual_information":"The corridor opens into a quiet off-white passage, while the figure keeps one hand on the gold rail and one hand relaxed at the side. The softened posture shows adaptation as an ongoing adjustment rather than a dramatic victory.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C04-B11","script_section":"S4","visual_information":"The figure pauses beside a stable corridor edge and turns slightly toward the peripheral presence. The gesture introduces meaningful connection as another condition that can support forward movement.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C04-B12","script_section":"S4","visual_information":"The gold handrail continues through the corridor while the figure's shadow becomes smaller and less distorted. The changing shadow suggests that accepting support can reduce strain without changing the person's core identity.","mode":"metaphor","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C04-B13","script_section":"S4","visual_information":"The figure passes from the dark threshold into a broader corridor while maintaining contact with the handrail. The expanded space visualizes several possible routes of adaptation beyond solitary endurance.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C04-B14","script_section":"S4","visual_information":"The figure stands between the gold handrail and the quiet second presence, with neither dominating the frame. The balanced arrangement shows resilience as the interaction of personal will and surrounding support.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C04-B15","script_section":"S4","visual_information":"The figure continues forward upright beside the steady gold handrail, leaving the unstable floor behind without looking back. The ending opens toward the idea that strength can follow multiple trajectories, including supported movement.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null}]}
